<title>UK: Merrydown first half profits slide.</title>
<headline>Merrydown first half profits slide.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended September 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		3.57		   vs 7.11</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 2.1		    vs 2.0</p>
<p> Pretax		     0.67		   vs 1.16</p>
<p> Turnover		  19.41		   vs 18.43</p>
<p> Operating result	 1.038		  vs 1.602</p>
<p> Interest		   0.365		  vs 0.443</p>
<p>Tax			  0.283		  vs 0.382</p>
<p> Pay date		   January 21</p>
<p>Div registration date  December 24 NOTE - UK drinks manufacturer and distributor Merrydown said despite the highly competitive marektplace, prospects for its branded ciders in the second half remain good. The &quot;alcopops&quot; market continues to grow but is also increasingly competitive. Revenue from Two Dogs brand was lower due to competition from over 90 new &quot;alcopop&quot; products since Two Dogs arrived in July 1995.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
